// Melts scrap into alloy, and eats charge doing it.
//
// **The room that finally gives scrap a consumer.** Scrap has been
// harvestable since M3 and dead-ended at the enclave's trade board,
// which is why `SYSTEMS.md` §3.11 could not answer whether stopping at a
// ruin is ever genuinely "it depends" — the answer was "yes, if you
// happen to be passing". With a forge aboard, a ruin is the input to
// both things that gate the tower's ceiling.
//
// It is also by far the largest charge sink in the game. A forge running
// flat out costs more across a day than continuous striding, so *running
// the forge* and *walking far* stop being separate decisions. That is
// the keystone doing its job (`DESIGN.md` §2 insight 2).
#![enable(implicit_some)]
RoomDef(
    id: "room.sun_forge",
    name: "Sun-forge",
    short: "FRG",
    // **Opens once the burner is lit**, which is where the opening
    // ends. `SYSTEMS.md` §6.11: a first-turn menu with twenty cards on
    // it is the loudest thing in the game and says nothing, so the menu
    // grows as the tower does. This is a fact about the tower, not the
    // player — the journal (§5.7) is the other kind of unlock and can
    // only filter a menu.
    // A forge without a rig has no scrap to refine. Reveal the metal
    // branch when the tower has actually committed to salvage.
    unlocked_by: "room.salvage_rig",
    category: Production,
    width: 2,
    // A salvage rig's price. If you are buying one you are probably
    // buying both, and the pair is what a ruin-going tower commits to.
    build_cost: [CostEntryDef(item: "item.poles", amount: 8)],
    // Four times the thornwright's 1. Sustained, that is 57,600 charge
    // across a full day — well over continuous striding's 2,880, and
    // more than two burners can feed without eating the mill's bamboo,
    // so a forge is something a tower runs in bursts and plans around
    // rather than leaves on.
    power_draw: 4,
    // Hotter than a burner and deliberately large enough that one
    // modest stack cannot carry two forges at once.
    exhaust_draw: 3,
    recipe: RecipeDef(
        // Eight seconds a bar: visibly the slowest thing in the chain,
        // which is what a forge should look like.
        craft_ticks: 240,
        inputs: [IoEntryDef(item: "item.scrap", amount: 3, buffer_max: 9)],
        outputs: [IoEntryDef(item: "item.alloy", amount: 1, buffer_max: 6)],
    ),
)
